.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-BUCKET-SET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-bucket-set - Connect or change the team's bucket


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team bucket set <team> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Save the bucket after Paperboat writes, reads back and deletes a small check object in it; a failing step is named and nothing is saved. Give the secret access key on standard input (--secret-access-key-stdin), never as an argument; leave it out to keep the stored key while changing another field.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--access-key-id\fP=""
	access key ID

.PP
\fB--bucket\fP=""
	bucket name

.PP
\fB--endpoint\fP=""
	https address of the S3 service, without a path

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for set

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--path-style\fP[=false]
	address the bucket in the URL path (MinIO and some other services)

.PP
\fB--prefix\fP=""
	optional folder inside the bucket

.PP
\fB--region\fP=""
	region of the bucket

.PP
\fB--secret-access-key-stdin\fP[=false]
	read the secret access key from standard input


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team-bucket(1)\fP
